# Build context is the meals/ workspace root, so ignore patterns are matched
# from there. Keep the image build hermetic and small by excluding installed
# deps, build output and dev/test artifacts from every copied tree.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.vite

# Tests, e2e and dev artifacts
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.screenshots
meals_client/apps/web/e2e

# Native app — not part of the web image, and pulling it in would drag in Expo
**/.expo
meals_client/apps/native

# Local env / secrets — production values are passed as build args
**/*.local
**/.env*.local

# VCS / OS / editor
**/.git
**/.DS_Store
**/*.orig

# Exception: the contract's committed dist/ IS needed (file: dependency), so it
# is re-included after the broad **/build and **/dist excludes above. The
# contract's own node_modules stays excluded — npm install reinstalls them.
#
# NOTE: the classic docker builder reads .dockerignore from the CONTEXT ROOT
# (the meals/ workspace dir), not from next to the Dockerfile. The effective
# copy therefore lives at meals/.dockerignore; this file is kept in sync as the
# documented intent and applies if anyone runs BuildKit with a per-Dockerfile
# ignore. Keep the two in sync.
!meals_model/build
!meals_model/build/typescript-package
!meals_model/build/typescript-package/**
meals_model/build/typescript-package/node_modules
